 "text": "Hey! How are you feeling? For everyday use, once a week or so is usually plenty. If you ride a lot on rough terrain, two or three times a month is better. There' a small valve in the tyre that needs to be opened slowly with a tyre lever. When you hear a hissing sound, it's right. Most people do. The valve on your pump will tell you the pressure, so stop when you hear hiss for the first time. Yes, a little. Lower the pressure a little so the tyre doesn't bubble, and then add more as needed.",
